window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-1ecd42c3fa49d659"]={"key":"ny_b1-1ecd42c3fa49d659","group":"ny_b1","uid":"1ecd42c3fa49d659","rank":55,"title":"private credit compliance recommendation 01","occupation":"financial_services_sales_agents","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Lorcan Toledano, a senior coverage officer at Rushmere Chambers, supporting the investment committee of Cobblemoor Networks’ client, the Aldbourne Foundation. The committee meets in nine days, on 12 December, and its chair, Ludmila Escamilla, wants a recommendation rather than another side-by-side product summary. The foundation has shortlisted two private-credit vehicles for a proposed $12 million allocation: Northmere Interval Credit Fund, an interval fund, and Harrowgate Private Credit BDC, a non-traded business development company. Valeria Dimitrov, Nadia Schuyler, and Kaia Havlicek will use the paper to challenge the recommendation at the meeting, so the document must make one clear call and show why that call remains defensible when the trade-offs are put under pressure. Use the supplied file investment_committee_packet.pdf as the sole source for product facts, performance figures, terms, governance information, and the committee’s recorded concerns; do not use live market information or add facts from memory. The packet shows that the quantified criteria do not point in one direction: the BDC is stronger on net yield and fee load, while the interval fund is stronger on redemption terms and leverage. It also records that the BDC’s founding credit officer left in June, that the successor has no full credit-cycle history, and that the foundation’s chair raised this informally as a possible reputational and key-person concern. Treat that concern as something the committee needs addressed without turning an informal comment into a verified allegation. Write recommendation_memo.docx and place it at the top level of the working directory you start in, using exactly that filename. Keep the memo to no more than three pages, make it suitable for a broad non-specialist audience, and choose exactly one vehicle for the proposed allocation. Explain the decision in plain language, distinguish observed facts from interpretation and uncertainty, show the main quantitative comparison and how the $12 million allocation relates to it, and make the chosen vehicle, decision date, and relevant assumptions easy to find. Before using the word “liquidity,” define what you mean by it in this memo, because committee members use that word both for the contractual ability to redeem and for the practical speed and certainty of receiving cash; do not use the term as though those meanings were interchangeable. The memo must also actively discourage the common mistake of reading a stated yield as a guaranteed or risk-free return, and it must not imply that either vehicle is insured, that repayment is assured, or that a historical or stated figure is a promise of future performance. Describe the principal risks and limitations that matter to the choice, including the governance or key-person issue, without presenting the chair’s informal concern as established misconduct or claiming certainty that the successor will underperform. State the principal basis on which the rejected vehicle loses, acknowledge the strongest case for it, and explain why the selected vehicle’s disadvantages are acceptable for this allocation under the source’s stated assumptions. Do not invent fees, yields, redemption windows, leverage ratios, ratings, legal protections, tax outcomes, portfolio holdings, regulatory conclusions, or diligence results that are not in the packet. Do not give individualized legal, tax, or investment advice beyond the committee recommendation, do not cite external rules, and do not finish with a list of future steps instead of the decision. The final paragraph should leave the committee with one unambiguous recommendation and the conditions or limitations that qualify it, while remaining a recommendation memo rather than a product brochure.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/investment_committee_packet.pdf` — Sole source for the two shortlisted vehicles’ quantitative terms, redemption and leverage features, governance facts, stated assumptions, and the committee’s recorded concern about the BDC credit officer transition.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `recommendation_memo.docx` — A concise compliance-oriented recommendation memo selecting exactly one of the two private-credit vehicles for the Aldbourne Foundation’s proposed $12 million allocation. (Top-level working directory; exact filename; no more than three pages; broad non-specialist readership; one recommendation only; use the supplied packet as the sole source for factual claims; define liquidity before using it; distinguish contractual redemption from practical cash access; actively caution against treating yield as guaranteed or risk-free; include quantitative comparison, risk treatment, uncertainty, and a clear final decision.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/investment_committee_packet.pdf","bytes":4137,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/216dc8abdf82b6acc67c9bdd09481d4f5607d3170c6373e026af074475fa8ff5.pdf","sha256":"216dc8abdf82b6acc67c9bdd09481d4f5607d3170c6373e026af074475fa8ff5","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"                                           Aldbourne Foundation\nInvestment Committee briefing | Private-credit shortlist | Prepared for the 12 December meeting\n\nPurpose. This briefing records the committee materials for a proposed $12,000,000 allocation. It compares two shortlisted\nvehicles only: Northmere Interval Credit Fund and Harrowgate Private Credit BDC. All figures below are supplied for committee\ncomparison; no recommendation is made in this packet.\n\nTerms used in this briefing\nNet yield is the stated annualized distribution rate shown below, net of the fee load shown below, as of 30 November. It is a\nstated rate, not a forecast. Fee load is the annual net operating-expense percentage supplied by each vehicle. Leverage is debt\ndivided by net assets as of 30 November; a lower figure is presented as lower leverage, not as a safety guarantee.\n\nProduct and quantitative comparison\n     Item                    Northmere Interval Credit Fund                        Harrowgate Private Credit BDC\n\n     Vehicle form            Interval fund: offers scheduled repurchase offers.    Non-traded BDC: not exchange-traded; offers a periodic share-redemp\n\n     Net yield               8.20% annualized distribution rate, net, as of 30 Nov 9.10% annualized distribution rate, net, as of 30 Nov\n\n     Fee load                2.30% annual net operating expenses                   1.80% annual net operating expenses\n\n     Redemption / repurchase\n                          Quarterly repurchase offers for up to 25% of NAV; 45-day\n                                                                                Quarterly\n                                                                                   notice redemption\n                                                                                          before the quarter-end\n                                                                                                      program forrepurchase\n                                                                                                                  up to 5% ofdate.\n                                                                                                                              NAV; 45-day notice befo\n\n     If requests exceed capacity\n                           Repurchase requests are accepted pro rata.              Redemption requests are accepted pro rata.\n\n     Leverage                0.25x debt / net assets as of 30 Nov                  0.65x debt / net assets as of 30 Nov\n\n\n\nInterpretive guardrail\nA redemption or repurchase request is a contractual mechanism, not a statement that cash will be received immediately or in\nfull: each program is periodic, subject to its stated capacity, notice period, and possible pro rata acceptance. The supplied terms\ntherefore make Northmere stronger on the contractual redemption comparison. The stated leverage figures make Northmere\nstronger on the leverage comparison. Harrowgate is stronger on the net-yield and fee-load comparisons.\n\nCommittee assumptions for this allocation\nThe proposed $12,000,000 allocation is intended as a five-year allocation. The Foundation does not expect to need this capital\nfor operating expenditure in the next 18 months. The committee has not set a minimum yield target. In selecting between\notherwise suitable shortlist candidates, it has asked that controlled contractual access to capital and continuity of investment\nleadership be weighed alongside stated income and cost.\n\nHarrowgate leadership transition and recorded concern\nHarrowgate’s founding credit officer left in June. The appointed successor has not yet managed a full credit cycle. At an informal\ndiscussion, Ludmila Escamilla, the Foundation chair, said that the transition could be a reputational and key-person concern for\nthe Foundation. This is a committee concern to address; the materials contain no finding or allegation of misconduct and do not\nestablish how the successor will perform.\n\nScope note\nThese are the supplied committee materials for the two shortlisted vehicles. They do not provide ratings, tax outcomes, legal\nconclusions, portfolio holdings, insurance or capital protection, or additional diligence results.\n\n\nRushmere Chambers coverage file | Issued 3 December | Internal committee materials\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/recommendation_memo.docx","bytes":40580,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/9bb588947813ebabfef39289bb52a5e60df1de264624220e4fb0697c5794974c.docx","sha256":"9bb588947813ebabfef39289bb52a5e60df1de264624220e4fb0697c5794974c","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Recommendation: Northmere Interval Credit Fund\nTo: Aldbourne Foundation Investment Committee  |  Decision date: 12 December  |  From: Lorcan Toledano, Senior Coverage Officer, Rushmere Chambers\nDecision. Allocate the proposed $12 million to Northmere Interval Credit Fund. Its lower stated yield and higher fee load are acceptable under the committee’s five-year, no-near-term-operating-cash assumption because its stronger contractual redemption terms, lower stated leverage, and no identified leadership-transition issue outweigh Harrowgate’s income-and-cost advantage for this allocation.\nScope, facts and meaning of “liquidity”\nSource and scope. This assessment relies only on the supplied investment committee packet; it is a committee recommendation, not legal, tax, or individualized investment advice. “Liquidity” in this memo has two separate meanings: (1) contractual redemption—the right and process to submit a repurchase or redemption request; and (2) practical access to cash—the speed and certainty of actually receiving cash. A contractual right is not immediate or certain cash access, especially where requests may be scaled back pro rata.\nPacket facts. Northmere Interval Credit Fund is an interval fund with quarterly repurchase offers; Harrowgate Private Credit BDC is a non-traded BDC with a periodic redemption program. Both require 45-day notice. Northmere offers up to 25% of net asset value (NAV) per quarter, while Harrowgate offers up to 5%; both are subject to pro rata acceptance if demand exceeds capacity. The packet therefore identifies Northmere as stronger on contractual redemption. It does not establish that either vehicle can deliver cash immediately or in full when requested.\nComparison and what the $12 million means\nPacket measure\nNorthmere\nHarrowgate\nStated net yield (annualized; 30 Nov)\n8.20%\n9.10%\nAnnual net operating-expense fee load\n2.30%\n1.80%\nQuarterly redemption / repurchase capacity\nUp to 25% of NAV\nUp to 5% of NAV\nLeverage (debt / net assets; 30 Nov)\n0.25x\n0.65x\nHow to read this comparison. On the proposed $12,000,000, the stated annualized net-yield figures correspond to approximately $984,000 for Northmere and $1,092,000 for Harrowgate—a $108,000 annualized difference. The stated fee-load percentages correspond to $276,000 and $216,000, respectively—a $60,000 difference. These illustrations show why Harrowgate’s yield and fee load matter, but they do not mechanically decide suitability. A stated or historical yield is not guaranteed, is not risk-free, and must not be read as a promise of future performance; neither vehicle is described in the packet as insured and repayment of principal is not assured. Lower leverage is a comparative characteristic, not a guarantee of safety or return.\nJudgment, risk and rejected alternative\nInterpretation. The packet’s assumptions are material: this is a five-year allocation, the Foundation does not expect to need the capital for operating expenditure over the next 18 months, and no minimum yield target has been set. Northmere’s 25% quarterly capacity does not remove practical cash-access risk, but it gives the Foundation a meaningfully broader contractual route if its cash needs change. The higher 2.30% fee load and lower 8.20% stated yield are the selected vehicle’s principal disadvantages; they are acceptable here because the committee asked to weigh controlled access to capital and leadership continuity alongside income and cost.\nHarrowgate’s strongest case—and why it loses. Harrowgate Private Credit BDC has the higher 9.10% stated net yield and lower 1.80% fee load, so it is the stronger income-and-cost choice on the packet’s figures. Its principal limitation for this allocation is not a finding about conduct or a prediction of performance. Rather, the packet records that its founding credit officer left in June and that the successor has no full credit-cycle history. The chair’s informal comment is an unverified reputational and key-person concern, not an allegation or evidence of misconduct. That uncertainty could prove immaterial and does not establish that the successor will underperform; nevertheless, when considered with Harrowgate’s narrower contractual redemption capacity and higher stated leverage, it is material enough to outweigh the $108,000 annualized yield illustration and $60,000 fee-load illustration.\nRecommendation. For the 12 December decision, I recommend allocating the proposed $12 million to Northmere Interval Credit Fund, subject to the packet’s stated five-year and no-near-term-operating-cash assumptions. It is not risk-free and cash is not available on demand; nevertheless, Northmere’s stronger contractual redemption terms, lower stated leverage, and absence of the identified Harrowgate key-person uncertainty make it the more defensible vehicle for this allocation.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A file named recommendation_memo.docx is present at the top level and opens as a valid Word document.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted working directory and document parse.","grader_hint":"Verify exact filename, location, and that the DOCX package is readable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered memo is no more than three pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document pagination.","grader_hint":"Render with a normal office-compatible engine and count pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies the Aldbourne Foundation as the decision-making client or committee.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo text.","grader_hint":"Look for the foundation name or an unambiguous equivalent."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies Rushmere Chambers as the preparer’s organisation or coverage context.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo text.","grader_hint":"Search the rendered text."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo states or clearly displays the proposed $12 million allocation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation amount in memo.","grader_hint":"Accept $12m, $12 million, or an unambiguous equivalent."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo selects exactly one of the two shortlisted vehicles as the recommendation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Headline, recommendation language, and conclusion.","grader_hint":"There must be one and only one recommended vehicle, not a tie or conditional choice between both."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo names both Northmere Interval Credit Fund and Harrowgate Private Credit BDC, or uses source-faithful unambiguous names for both.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Product references.","grader_hint":"Check that both products are identifiable, not merely described as Fund A and Fund B."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies the decision as being for the committee meeting on 12 December or otherwise gives the relevant decision date from the brief.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening metadata or body.","grader_hint":"Accept an explicit 12 December reference."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommendation is visible early enough that a committee reader can find the decision without reading the entire memo.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered memo structure.","grader_hint":"Judge whether the recommendation is in a title, executive summary, or opening paragraph rather than buried."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo reports the packet’s quantitative comparison without reversing which vehicle is stronger on net yield.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison prose or table against packet.","grader_hint":"The BDC must be identified as the higher-net-yield option according to the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo reports the packet’s fee-load comparison without reversing which vehicle is stronger on fee load.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison prose or table against packet.","grader_hint":"The BDC must be identified as the lower-fee-load option according to the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo reports the packet’s redemption comparison without reversing which vehicle is stronger on redemption terms.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison prose or table against packet.","grader_hint":"The interval fund must be identified as stronger on the packet’s redemption comparison."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo reports the packet’s leverage comparison without reversing which vehicle is stronger on leverage.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison prose or table against packet.","grader_hint":"The interval fund must be identified as stronger on leverage under the packet’s stated comparison."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo uses the packet’s actual quantitative figures accurately wherever it reproduces them.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All reproduced figures compared with source.","grader_hint":"Check every yield, fee, redemption, leverage, and allocation figure for transcription accuracy."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not present a quantitative scorecard as automatically deciding the recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reasoning connecting comparison to decision.","grader_hint":"Credit only if the memo weighs, rather than mechanically totals, the criteria."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo defines liquidity before relying on the term in its analysis.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"First substantive use and preceding definition.","grader_hint":"The definition must precede or be integrated into the first analytical use, not appear only in a footnote after repeated use."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The liquidity definition distinguishes contractual redemption ability from practical speed or certainty of receiving cash.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Liquidity definition.","grader_hint":"Both dimensions must be explicitly distinguished."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not treat contractual redemption terms and practical cash access as interchangeable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Liquidity discussion.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit qualification or separate treatment of the two meanings."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo links the selected vehicle’s liquidity assessment to the allocation’s needs or time horizon without claiming certainty beyond the packet.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision rationale.","grader_hint":"The analysis must explain relevance, not merely recite terms."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo expressly states that yield is not a guaranteed return.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Yield caution.","grader_hint":"Accept clear equivalent wording such as not promised, not assured, or not guaranteed."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo expressly states or strongly conveys that yield should not be read as risk-free.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Yield caution.","grader_hint":"A generic risk disclosure without connecting it to yield is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo actively discourages the common misuse of treating a stated or historical yield as a promise of future performance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Plain-language warning in memo.","grader_hint":"Judge whether the language would correct a reader’s mistaken inference, rather than merely avoid making the mistake itself."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not imply that either vehicle is insured.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All product descriptions and disclosures.","grader_hint":"Search for insurance, insured, principal protection, or equivalent claims and assess context."},{"rubric_item_id":"r24","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not imply that repayment of principal is assured.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Risk language.","grader_hint":"Do not award if the memo uses unconditional capital-preservation language."},{"rubric_item_id":"r25","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not imply that historical performance guarantees future performance.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Performance discussion.","grader_hint":"Check for appropriate limitations around historical or stated figures."},{"rubric_item_id":"r26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies the BDC founding credit officer’s June departure as a packet-supported fact.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Governance discussion against packet.","grader_hint":"The event and timing must be accurately stated."},{"rubric_item_id":"r27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies that the successor lacks a full credit-cycle history, as supported by the packet.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Governance discussion against packet.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording that conveys no completed full-cycle record."},{"rubric_item_id":"r28","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo treats the leadership transition as a key-person or governance risk relevant to the recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Risk analysis.","grader_hint":"The issue must affect the decision analysis, not be a disconnected background fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"r29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo distinguishes the foundation chair’s informal concern from a verified allegation or finding.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Wording of concern discussion.","grader_hint":"Look for attribution and qualification such as concern, signal, or issue for consideration, without converting it into misconduct."},{"rubric_item_id":"r30","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not claim the successor will underperform or that the transition proves a loss.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Governance conclusion.","grader_hint":"Credit only when uncertainty remains bounded."},{"rubric_item_id":"r31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo explains how the key-person concern was weighed against the quantitative criteria.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Integrated recommendation reasoning.","grader_hint":"A mere list of the concern and figures earns no credit; the trade-off must be explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"r32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo makes a clear, defensible call despite the split quantitative criteria and governance concern.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole memo.","grader_hint":"Assess whether the conclusion follows from stated priorities and evidence rather than from unsupported preference."},{"rubric_item_id":"r33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo states the strongest case for the rejected vehicle fairly and accurately.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rejected-option discussion against packet.","grader_hint":"The rejected option’s strongest relevant advantages must be acknowledged, not caricatured."},{"rubric_item_id":"r34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo states the principal reason the rejected vehicle loses for this allocation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision rationale.","grader_hint":"The document must identify a decisive basis, not leave the rejection unexplained."},{"rubric_item_id":"r35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo explains why the selected vehicle’s disadvantages are acceptable under the packet’s assumptions.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Selected-option discussion.","grader_hint":"Require a reasoned acceptance of drawbacks, not an assertion that they do not exist."},{"rubric_item_id":"r36","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo separates facts from interpretation, judgment, or recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Language and structure.","grader_hint":"Look for attribution, labels, or visibly distinct factual and analytical passages."},{"rubric_item_id":"r37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies the assumptions that materially support the recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assumptions section or integrated analysis.","grader_hint":"Assumptions must be tied to the choice and drawn from the packet or clearly marked as assumptions."},{"rubric_item_id":"r38","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not present an unverified external fact as though it came from the packet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claim audit against sole source.","grader_hint":"Check claims about products, markets, legal status, performance, and governance for source support or qualification."},{"rubric_item_id":"r39","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not invent fees, yields, redemption windows, leverage ratios, ratings, legal protections, tax outcomes, holdings, or diligence results.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claim audit against packet.","grader_hint":"Any unsupported invented item fails this criterion."},{"rubric_item_id":"r40","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies the source packet or makes clear that product facts are drawn from the supplied committee materials.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source note or attribution.","grader_hint":"Accept a concise source note."},{"rubric_item_id":"r41","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not cite external jurisdiction-specific rules as the basis of the recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Citations and legal claims.","grader_hint":"No outside statutory or regulatory conclusion should be introduced."},{"rubric_item_id":"r42","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo avoids individualized legal or tax advice beyond the product recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope of advice.","grader_hint":"A bounded limitation is preferred where relevant."},{"rubric_item_id":"r43","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo explains why the allocation size matters to the comparison or risk discussion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Allocation analysis.","grader_hint":"The $12 million must be used analytically, not merely repeated."},{"rubric_item_id":"r44","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any arithmetic involving the $12 million allocation and packet figures is correct within ±$1,000 or ±0.1 percentage points, as applicable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo calculations checked against source.","grader_hint":"Only apply the relevant tolerance to calculations actually shown."},{"rubric_item_id":"r45","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo’s quantitative comparison preserves the packet’s units, periods, and definitions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tables and prose against packet.","grader_hint":"Check that annual, net, gross, fee, leverage, and redemption measures are not silently relabeled."},{"rubric_item_id":"r46","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo qualifies uncertainty where the packet does not establish a future outcome.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Risk and performance language.","grader_hint":"Look for calibrated terms such as may, could, subject to, or not established, used appropriately."},{"rubric_item_id":"r47","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies the selected vehicle’s principal risks rather than presenting the recommendation as one-sided.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Risk discussion.","grader_hint":"At least the material trade-offs from the packet should be named and connected to the decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"r48","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies the rejected vehicle’s principal relevant risk or limitation, including the governance issue where applicable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rejected-option discussion.","grader_hint":"The rejection must be risk-based or limitation-based, not merely preference-based."},{"rubric_item_id":"r49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The language is understandable to a broad non-specialist audience without requiring the reader to decode unexplained product jargon.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered memo readability.","grader_hint":"Assess definitions, plain-language explanations, and whether acronyms or technical terms are controlled."},{"rubric_item_id":"r50","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo explains or defines the relevant difference between an interval fund and a non-traded BDC sufficiently for the decision context.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Product comparison.","grader_hint":"A short functional explanation is sufficient; do not require external legal detail."},{"rubric_item_id":"r51","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not describe either product as liquid without the defined qualification and supporting context.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Liquidity terminology audit.","grader_hint":"Unqualified labels such as highly liquid should not appear."},{"rubric_item_id":"r52","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo connects redemption terms to the practical risk of needing cash, without equating a redemption right with immediate cash.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Liquidity analysis.","grader_hint":"Require both contractual and practical treatment."},{"rubric_item_id":"r53","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo avoids overstating the significance of leverage as a guarantee of safety or return.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Leverage discussion.","grader_hint":"Leverage must be treated as a comparative characteristic with risk implications, not as proof of quality."},{"rubric_item_id":"r54","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo explains why net yield and fee load are relevant but insufficient alone to determine suitability.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Quantitative reasoning.","grader_hint":"The memo must integrate non-quantitative considerations."},{"rubric_item_id":"r55","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo includes a concise limitations or scope statement about reliance on the supplied packet.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo disclosure.","grader_hint":"Accept a source-limitation statement that does not undermine the recommendation unnecessarily."},{"rubric_item_id":"r56","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not assert that the chair’s informal concern is evidence of misconduct, fraud, or regulatory breach.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Governance wording.","grader_hint":"Search for unsupported allegations and assess the surrounding qualification."},{"rubric_item_id":"r57","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo is professionally usable at the committee meeting: concise, internally consistent, appropriately caveated, and easy to challenge constructively.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole rendered artifact.","grader_hint":"Judge practical usability, not ornamentation; technical correctness that leaves the reader unable to identify the call should not pass."},{"rubric_item_id":"r58","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The final paragraph contains one unambiguous recommendation and does not end with a next-steps list.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final paragraph.","grader_hint":"The ending must be the decision, with qualifications if needed, rather than an action-plan sequence."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"A senior financial-services coverage professional is preparing a defensible investment-vehicle recommendation for a foundation committee. The work requires bounded doctrinal language around product claims, uncertainty, liquidity terminology, and non-guaranteed returns while still making one commercially useful decision.","difficulty_sources":["Selecting one recommendation when quantitative criteria split across the two vehicles.","Weighing an informal, unverified key-person concern without converting it into an allegation or prediction.","Defining and consistently applying the two meanings of liquidity.","Actively preventing yield from being misread as guaranteed or risk-free.","Producing a source-faithful doctrinal memo for non-specialists within a three-page cap."],"authoring_plan":{"source_file":{"filename":"investment_committee_packet.pdf","purpose":"Create one self-contained offline committee packet containing complete, mutually consistent information for both vehicles and the recorded concern. Include exact figures for net yield, fee load, redemption terms, leverage, and the $12 million allocation; identify the interval fund as stronger on redemption terms and leverage and the non-traded BDC as stronger on net yield and fee load. Include the June departure of the BDC founding credit officer, the successor’s lack of a full credit-cycle history, and the foundation chair’s informal concern, carefully worded as an unverified governance/key-person concern. Include enough definitions and stated assumptions for accurate comparison, but no external legal rule or hidden local code.","construction_constraints":["Use synthetic product and organisation materials only.","Ensure every fact needed by the rubric is present in this one source.","Make all arithmetic derivable from source values.","Do not seed contradictory facts or defects; difficulty is judgment and disciplined doctrinal writing, not error finding.","The source should support either a reasoned recommendation if the solver weighs the trade-offs coherently, while making unsupported claims unreachable."]},"gold_derivation":{"decision_logic":"Prepare a reference memo that chooses one vehicle, fairly acknowledges the other vehicle’s quantified advantages, treats liquidity as both contractual redemption and practical cash access, treats yield as non-guaranteed, and weighs the BDC leadership transition as an uncertain but material key-person/reputational risk rather than misconduct. The gold is passed when the recommendation is source-faithful, internally consistent, clearly bounded, and usable by a non-specialist committee.","required_vocabulary":["liquidity","contractual redemption","practical access to cash","not guaranteed","not risk-free","key-person risk","uncertainty","recommendation"],"doctrinal_pairs":[["Define liquidity before analysis","Do not conflate redemption rights with immediate cash"],["State yield comparison","Do not present yield as guaranteed, insured, or risk-free"],["Report June departure and successor experience limitation","Do not assert misconduct or predict underperformance"],["Make one recommendation","Do not end with two equal options or an unresolved next-steps list"],["Use packet assumptions","Do not invent external facts, legal conclusions, tax outcomes, ratings, or diligence results"]],"quality_checks":["Render the reference DOCX and confirm it fits within three pages.","Check all figures against the source and recalculate any displayed dollar or percentage arithmetic.","Check that the first analytical use of liquidity follows an explicit definition.","Check that the final paragraph names exactly one vehicle.","Check that the memo remains a recommendation rather than a comparison-only brochure."]},"solver_instance":{"inputs_complete":true,"method_left_to_solver":true,"transformation":"Read and extract the sole packet, compare the two vehicles, calculate or restructure only as needed, and author a bounded recommendation memo.","intended_verdict":"A competent financial-services practitioner can produce a defensible memo offline from the packet; the decisive quality is disciplined weighing and non-overclaiming, not discovery of missing data."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"investment_committee_packet","filename":"investment_committee_packet.pdf","purpose":"Sole source for the two shortlisted vehicles’ quantitative terms, redemption and leverage features, governance facts, stated assumptions, and the committee’s recorded concern about the BDC credit officer transition.","required":true,"discovery":"Read this file before drafting; no other factual source is supplied or permitted."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"recommendation_memo","filename":"recommendation_memo.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise compliance-oriented recommendation memo selecting exactly one of the two private-credit vehicles for the Aldbourne Foundation’s proposed $12 million allocation.","required":true,"constraints":["Top-level working directory; exact filename; no more than three pages; broad non-specialist readership; one recommendation only; use the supplied packet as the sole source for factual claims; define liquidity before using it; distinguish contractual redemption from practical cash access; actively caution against treating yield as guaranteed or risk-free; include quantitative comparison, risk treatment, uncertainty, and a clear final decision."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"financial_services_sales_agents","sector":"finance_insurance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":3.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have a domain-experienced reviewer validate the recommendation logic and doctrinal boundaries against the supplied packet, then have an independent reviewer check page count, source fidelity, terminology order, arithmetic, and whether the final call is unambiguous.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The recommendation direction is intentionally not fixed in the request; either vehicle can be the gold choice if the memo accurately weighs the packet’s trade-offs and reaches one defensible conclusion. Relational checks should be applied to the source facts actually reproduced."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:54:00+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:54:00+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:54:00+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:54:00+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['r35', 'r39']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:54:00+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/1ecd42c3fa49d659","declared_deliverables":["recommendation_memo.docx"]};
